{"title":"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The limit of the sum of an infinite number of terms in a geometric progression is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/a/d1a02c35527881dca09732d75ab40709b60646ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {a}{1 - r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"42\" height=\"33\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> denotes the first term and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/8/648b9e311b0dc4b3602eb9b152761143fa974532.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$- 1 &lt; r &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"88\" height=\"12\" /> denotes the common ratio. The limit of the sum of their squares is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/7/4f7353379ae5fae8b9a9b74a64feb514951577a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac {a^2}{(1 - r)^2} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac {a^2}{1 + r^2} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac {a^2}{1 - r^2} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac {4a^2}{1 + r^2} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{none of these}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"621\" height=\"45\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The original series is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/d/58dda8475b8bd5bab159bb18b19752f2ed853750.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + ar + ar^2 + ar^3 + \\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"194\" height=\"18\" />, so the new series is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/c/3aca17b4c5434e395d84cf4e3b62bbd842eb9b39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 + a^2r^2 +a^2r^4 +a^2r^6+\\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"232\" height=\"18\" />.  The new series is an infinite geometric series with first term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/9/9698c992334be77221be8c8c819909eca34fde9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> and common ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/2/e2221c84f16a3f75ae07e5023384cc40d9c05357.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^2$\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" />, so its sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/e/e0ee1814b50492437aa655cfb51521999aaf5a26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac {a^2}{1 - r^2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"97\" height=\"52\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME\" title=\"1951 AHSME\">1951 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1951 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"h